{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-69727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5}{4})=(\\frac{4}{3})+[]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-69727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\frac{5}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{5}{4})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{5}{4})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5}{4})=(\\frac{4}{3})+(\\frac{4}{4})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{4}{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-69727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f600b0c2918660e3239a6059afd4087f22721af1290b313b939b332404c73892"} {"question" "q-69727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-69727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{3}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{3}{2})"] ["math" "(\\frac{4}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{4}{4})"] ["math" "(\\frac{5}{3})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-69727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{4}{4})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{4}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{3!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f600b0c2918660e3239a6059afd4087f22721af1290b313b939b332404c73892"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "56"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-70313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-113610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{4}{2})=[]+(\\frac{3}{2})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-113610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\frac{4}{2}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $4$ and position $2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{4}{2})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{4}{2})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{4}{2})=(\\frac{3}{1})+(\\frac{3}{2})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{3}{1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-113610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f600b0c2918660e3239a6059afd4087f22721af1290b313b939b332404c73892"} {"question" "q-113610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-f