 (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\frac{6}{0}) &  & (\\frac{6}{1}) &  & (\\frac{6}{2}) &  & (\\frac{6}{3}) &  & (\\frac{6}{4}) &  & (\\frac{6}{5}) &  & (\\frac{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{6}{4})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{4})=(\\frac{5}{3})+(\\frac{5}{4})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{5}{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-113611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f600b0c2918660e3239a6059afd4087f22721af1290b313b939b332404c73892"} {"question" "q-113611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995308/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bfc370215497f14d57dabb00b1c074d0013ffa1a2377c302bd77ca57ab8c30f"} {"question" "q-113611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{4}{3})"] ["math" "(\\frac{4}{4})"] ["math" "(\\frac{5}{3})"] ["math" "(\\frac{5}{5})"] ["math" "(\\frac{6}{5})"]] "